    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0329" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5253: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September 22,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 9:24 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>From [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>393, September 20, noon. General Siberian advance along whole front still
                    continues. Uprisings in European Russia at Tambov and Kozlov assuming large
                    proportions. It appears that it will shortly <pb facs="0330" n="218"
                        xml:id="pg218"/> unite with Denekine front cutting off many Bolsheviki and
                    advancing Denekine half way to Moscow from its [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >his</hi>] present position. Harris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
